          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l21",
          "reminder": "Geometric regions can be combined or subtracted when their boundaries and shared interval are identified."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Match the requested expression",
      "body": "<p>Compare the input of your inverse with the input appearing in the requested integrand. Look for a horizontal reflection preserving the interval.</p>",
      "recap": "Track the input interval when reflecting a graph; a reflection can preserve area while rearranging the heights.",
      "pitfall": "The target is not the inverse expression with the input left unchanged.",
      "pause": "Use the interval-preserving transformation to obtain the requested integral.",
      "recall": [
